WEBVTT

﻿1

00:04:14.255 --> 00:04:23.698
And all I have to do today


00:04:24.598 --> 00:04:34.041
Is get past remembering...


00:04:38.546 --> 00:04:39.888
Maybe.


00:04:41.749 --> 00:04:43.894
Just this once.


00:04:45.519 --> 00:04:49.159
Let me think about
it a little bit. Okay?


00:05:19.053 --> 00:05:21.999
Hi, Tina.


00:05:25.559 --> 00:05:27.436
Something happened?


00:05:27.561 --> 00:05:30.302
No. I just didn't want
to come this year.


00:05:34.134 --> 00:05:36.807
'Cause it's her thirteenth birthday.


00:05:40.975 --> 00:05:42.783
I guess.


00:05:43.177 --> 00:05:44.849
I understand.


00:05:55.456 --> 00:05:59.028
I hate living in that house alone.


00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:09.972
I miss Matthew.


00:06:12.439 --> 00:06:14.612
I miss Cassandra.


00:06:19.613 --> 00:06:21.615
I miss living.


00:07:21.108 --> 00:07:22.809
Going into town?


00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:23.947
Yeah.


00:07:24.278 --> 00:07:25.950
All right.


00:07:27.748 --> 00:07:30.250
- It's cold out there, huh?
- Sure is.


00:07:35.756 --> 00:07:38.451
- I'm Matt.
- Page.


00:07:38.552 --> 00:07:39.791
- What's your name?
- Page.


00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:43.072
Page. Nice to meet you, Page.


00:08:49.229 --> 00:08:51.140
- Thanks.
- Yeah.


00:09:15.522 --> 00:09:16.823
Hi.


00:09:16.824 --> 00:09:18.962
Hey. What's up?


00:09:19.493 --> 00:09:20.971
Not much.


00:09:21.395 --> 00:09:23.067
Planning on going?


00:09:23.197 --> 00:09:25.005
Well, aren't you?


00:09:25.098 --> 00:09:27.669
She said she wanted to
meet with both of us.


00:09:29.736 --> 00:09:34.309
Well, it is... it's dumping up here.
How is it down there?


00:09:35.943 --> 00:09:38.110
No, it's fine. It's clear.


00:09:38.111 --> 00:09:40.648
There's no way that I'm
going to get down there.


00:09:41.315 --> 00:09:43.920
It's okay. You always
have excuses, Matthew.


00:09:44.384 --> 00:09:46.022
Yeah.


00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:50.790
Do you remember that brush
that she used to love?


00:09:50.791 --> 00:09:53.464
- The one that my mum gave her?
- Yeah.


00:09:53.794 --> 00:09:55.705
Well, I just found one.


00:09:56.463 --> 00:09:58.064
It... it's almost the same.


00:09:58.065 --> 00:09:59.339
Where?


00:09:59.533 --> 00:10:00.933
One of the rooms.


00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:02.970
Someone must have left it.


00:10:03.103 --> 00:10:04.741
That's weird.


00:10:05.305 --> 00:10:07.148
Yeah, it's weird.


00:10:09.309 --> 00:10:11.345
I should get back to work.


00:10:11.411 --> 00:10:13.185
Okay. I love you.


00:10:13.514 --> 00:10:15.152
Love you.


00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.710
I really feel like...


00:10:44.711 --> 00:10:47.680
I have been cracking the
whip here on them, okay.


00:10:47.681 --> 00:10:50.783
But if there is any chance of
us finishing this on time, I...


00:10:50.784 --> 00:10:54.493
You will. Which you will 'cause it's
your job to make sure we finish on time.


00:10:55.155 --> 00:10:56.676
I mean,


00:10:56.677 --> 00:11:00.359
how old were you when you first
started working for me as a welder,


00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:01.827
how old were you?


00:11:01.828 --> 00:11:03.496
- Fifteen.
- Fifteen.


00:11:03.497 --> 00:11:06.978
And in all those years did I
ever treat you like a friend?


00:11:07.901 --> 00:11:09.535
Never!


00:11:09.536 --> 00:11:13.339
Now I might have treated you like a son,
but I never treated you like a friend.


00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:16.142
That's the problem here, Mika.
You're treating all these guys


00:11:16.143 --> 00:11:19.988
like they're your buddies
and they're not.


00:11:22.816 --> 00:11:24.795
They're tradesmen.


00:11:26.253 --> 00:11:29.859
They're working for you.
They're not your friend.


00:11:35.862 --> 00:11:37.363
Hey there.


00:11:37.931 --> 00:11:39.865
This is a... this is a
beautiful development.


00:11:39.866 --> 00:11:42.535
We... we sold out the first
phase in a couple of days.


00:11:42.536 --> 00:11:45.471
And you jump in now you can have
your place on the ninth hole.


00:11:45.472 --> 00:11:46.439
Vince Grey.


00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:50.178
Detective Cornwall. Hi. I'd like to...


00:11:50.677 --> 00:11:53.589
I'd like to ask you some questions
about your charity ball.


00:11:54.314 --> 00:11:56.157
Still no word?


00:12:00.053 --> 00:12:04.057
Well, I... I gave a statement
to one of your colleagues and...


00:12:04.191 --> 00:12:07.159
Listen, we can do this here or
we can go down to the station.


00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.900
Wherever you want.


00:12:08.962 --> 00:12:11.965
Hey, okay. Sure. Sit down.


00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:16.102
The woman that offered Detective
Dunlop a ride, had you seen her before?


00:12:16.103 --> 00:12:18.139
- No.
- You'd never seen her?


00:12:18.872 --> 00:12:20.350
No.


00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:23.216
I had not. How do you know that...


00:12:23.877 --> 00:12:28.792
Detective Dunlop's disappearance
is connected to this woman?


00:12:29.349 --> 00:12:31.658
Did... did I say it was?


00:12:32.419 --> 00:12:36.025
Look, I've... I've already
made a statement.


00:12:36.256 --> 00:12:39.703
- I've already talked to a detective.
- Right.


00:12:40.494 --> 00:12:43.998
I mean, I... I really, I don't know
how I can help you more than that.


00:12:45.499 --> 00:12:48.411
Your wife is on the board
of this charity, correct?


00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:53.314
- Yeah.
- Well, I'd like to speak to her, if I can.


00:12:53.573 --> 00:12:54.974
Well, be my guest.


00:12:54.975 --> 00:12:58.251
Well, she won't return any of my
phone calls. I've tried many times.


00:12:59.579 --> 00:13:02.491
- I'll make sure that she does.
- Good. Thank you.


00:13:02.516 --> 00:13:04.086
One more thing.


00:13:04.451 --> 00:13:07.787
A guest reported seeing the two
of you having a conversation.


00:13:07.788 --> 00:13:10.700
- What was that about?
- I made a comment


00:13:11.024 --> 00:13:13.793
to her about how different she looked...


00:13:13.794 --> 00:13:16.900
that night from how she
appears in this picture.


00:13:19.866 --> 00:13:21.936
Is that why you kept it?


00:13:22.536 --> 00:13:25.371
You were seen having a
conversation in front of it.


00:13:25.372 --> 00:13:27.044
Before she went missing.


00:13:27.174 --> 00:13:28.778
Why don't you take it?


00:13:32.546 --> 00:13:34.150
Take 'em both.


00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:50.203
Is there any hope of the two
of you getting back together?


00:13:50.731 --> 00:13:54.576
We talk. He calls, you know,
all the time.


00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.579
It's like one big talk.


00:14:01.842 --> 00:14:04.049
Talks me to sleep sometimes.


00:14:07.547 --> 00:14:10.027
But he's scared to show his face.


00:14:10.784 --> 00:14:12.126
Why?


00:14:12.452 --> 00:14:14.192
'Cause he's guilty.


00:14:15.155 --> 00:14:16.929
Because it's his fault.


00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.363
This whole thing is his fault.


00:14:22.929 --> 00:14:25.409
You know, I want him to feel guilty.


00:14:28.869 --> 00:14:30.814
It makes sense.


00:14:35.308 --> 00:14:37.253
Nothing else does.


00:14:49.456 --> 00:14:51.299
That cowboy?


00:14:51.758 --> 00:14:53.168
Yeah.


00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:58.300
Come on in.


00:15:01.601 --> 00:15:02.935
Thank you.


00:15:02.936 --> 00:15:05.416
- Detective Jeffrey Cornwall.
- Hi.


00:15:05.572 --> 00:15:07.142
Yeah, Jeff.


00:15:12.179 --> 00:15:15.147
You have an impressive
clearance rate, Detective Cornwall.


00:15:15.148 --> 00:15:16.524
Thank you.


00:15:18.318 --> 00:15:22.388
Why would you walk away from a great
career in homicide to join my unit?


00:15:22.389 --> 00:15:25.062
Well, I figure it's pretty
much the same skill set.


00:15:25.492 --> 00:15:28.029
Except here I get to deal
with living victims,


00:15:28.595 --> 00:15:31.530
- for a change.
- What is your history with children?


00:15:31.531 --> 00:15:33.874
Well, I was one, once.


00:15:37.704 --> 00:15:40.241
Have you ever felt attracted to them?


00:15:41.107 --> 00:15:42.441
No.


00:15:42.442 --> 00:15:45.047
Do you have a fantasy life?


00:15:49.449 --> 00:15:51.792
What does your fantasy life involve?


00:15:52.519 --> 00:15:54.123
Adult females.


00:15:54.187 --> 00:15:56.928
Brown hair, blue eyes.


00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:58.560
Single?


00:15:58.592 --> 00:16:00.435
Yes.


00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.038
Dating?


00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:05.941
No, I haven't been in a
relationship in a while.


00:16:07.601 --> 00:16:09.205
Why is that?


00:16:09.436 --> 00:16:11.506
It's less complicated.


00:16:17.077 --> 00:16:18.988
Take a seat.


00:16:22.816 --> 00:16:26.820
So here's what we are dealing with.


00:16:28.588 --> 00:16:30.032
Ready?


00:16:30.056 --> 00:16:31.364
Yeah.


00:16:51.778 --> 00:16:54.189
Jesus Christ!


00:16:58.451 --> 00:17:01.659
We look at images and
videos like that every day.


00:17:01.821 --> 00:17:04.232
Kids being abused...


00:17:05.759 --> 00:17:08.899
and tortured online while others watch.


00:17:09.529 --> 00:17:13.806
Our job is to not look away.


00:17:16.336 --> 00:17:20.172
The people who do that to kids...


00:17:20.173 --> 00:17:22.141
- Pedophiles.
- I want to stop them.


00:17:22.142 --> 00:17:25.179
You want to shoot them?
Beat them up? Put them in the ground?


00:17:25.412 --> 00:17:27.255
I want to stop 'em.


00:17:35.655 --> 00:17:38.931
Internet technology keeps leaping ahead.


00:17:38.959 --> 00:17:41.166
We're always playing catch-up.


00:17:42.429 --> 00:17:44.567
Sometimes the only way


00:17:44.631 --> 00:17:48.476
to find a needle in the haystack
is one straw at a time.


00:17:53.073 --> 00:17:56.417
Sam, our computer geek.
Mike, from Drugs.


00:17:56.509 --> 00:17:59.011
Everyone, this is Detective
Jeffrey Cornwall.


00:17:59.546 --> 00:18:03.382
You've already met Frank.
He is old school.


00:18:03.383 --> 00:18:06.090
- Young at heart.
- Yeah but, old everywhere else.


00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:10.656
And that's Teddy.
He has a very particular skill:


00:18:10.657 --> 00:18:12.491
visual pattern recognition.


00:18:12.492 --> 00:18:14.560
Teddy has an eye for detail.


00:18:14.561 --> 00:18:16.528
- Wanna show him, Teddy?
- No, I don't, Sam.


00:18:16.529 --> 00:18:17.730
I wish you would stop
doing this every time


00:18:17.731 --> 00:18:19.131
- someone new comes in the office.
- Come on.


00:18:19.132 --> 00:18:21.433
Come on, come on, come on. Come on.


00:18:21.434 --> 00:18:23.277
- All right.
- All right.


00:18:25.905 --> 00:18:31.787
Okay, it's like an old stone building.
It's a church or a castle or something.


00:18:32.946 --> 00:18:35.114
With a bridge going over a river.


00:18:35.115 --> 00:18:38.550
There's a woman standing on
the bridge in a beige coat,


00:18:38.551 --> 00:18:40.689
holding a red umbrella.


00:18:45.492 --> 00:18:46.692
That's impressive.


00:18:46.693 --> 00:18:49.695
Not really. Practice and guess work.


00:18:49.696 --> 00:18:51.504
Could have been a red kite.


00:18:52.232 --> 00:18:55.906
- So what's your deal, Jeff?
- Me?


00:18:56.336 --> 00:18:57.736
I arrest people.


00:18:57.737 --> 00:18:59.944
All right. Sounds good.


00:19:34.307 --> 00:19:36.809
- Promise.
- I promise.


00:19:37.577 --> 00:19:39.215
Pinkie promise.


00:19:39.345 --> 00:19:42.587
Okay. Pinkie promise.


00:19:43.416 --> 00:19:46.795
Cass, say bye to Albert, honey.
We gotta go.


00:19:47.053 --> 00:19:48.454
- Bye.
- Bye, Albert!


00:19:48.455 --> 00:19:50.093
- Bye!
- Bye, buddy.


00:19:51.591 --> 00:19:53.158
What were you guys talking about?


00:19:53.159 --> 00:19:55.427
I made him promise,
he'll never skate with anyone else.


00:19:55.428 --> 00:19:57.463
- Nobody else, ever as long as he lives?
- Nobody else.


00:19:57.464 --> 00:19:58.831
- Wow, that's a...
- That's a big promise.


00:19:58.832 --> 00:20:02.134
- For your whole life?
- Yeah. We're a team.


00:20:02.135 --> 00:20:04.979
- There's my girl. But we gotta go.
- Yeah. Bye.


00:20:05.071 --> 00:20:06.709
Come here.


00:20:09.242 --> 00:20:10.509
Okay, I'll see you at home. Love you!


00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:11.610
Bye!


00:20:11.611 --> 00:20:14.057
- Bye!
- Bye! I Bye!


00:20:28.561 --> 00:20:30.395
But the fact that you
guys made that promise


00:20:30.396 --> 00:20:31.997
to each other,
promise to always be a team,


00:20:31.998 --> 00:20:35.033
it means you have to start thinking
about how you present yourselves, okay?


00:20:35.034 --> 00:20:38.014
It's... it's... I'm just saying
that it's not necessary.


00:20:38.271 --> 00:20:40.839
You guys are so good
it's actually distracting.


00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:43.475
Albert thinks it makes us stand out.


00:20:43.476 --> 00:20:46.378
I don't think so. I think what makes
you stand out is your talent.


00:20:46.379 --> 00:20:49.792
Whether you got a white skate on one
foot and a black on the other it's...


00:20:51.451 --> 00:20:53.118
What's the... what's the
word I'm thinking of?


00:20:53.119 --> 00:20:55.187
- Irrelevant?
- Irrelevant. Right.


00:20:55.188 --> 00:20:56.588
Irrelevant.


00:20:56.589 --> 00:20:58.659
It's like a trick you don't need.


00:20:58.758 --> 00:21:01.135
- A trick?
- Yeah, exactly.


00:21:01.427 --> 00:21:05.130
- What's so funny?
- No, it's not a trick, it's a gimmick.


00:21:05.131 --> 00:21:07.533
- A gimmick we don't need.
- It's a gimmick you don't need.


00:21:07.534 --> 00:21:08.600
- A gimmick.
- Well, there you go.


00:21:08.601 --> 00:21:09.935
- It's the proper word.
- Oh, that's the proper word?


00:21:09.936 --> 00:21:12.712
- Yeah. Gimmick is the proper word.
- Thank you.


00:21:20.079 --> 00:21:21.421
Hello.


00:21:21.748 --> 00:21:24.650
Hi. Sarah called in sick.
I might be really late.


00:21:24.651 --> 00:21:25.993
Ouch.


00:21:26.586 --> 00:21:28.861
I don't know what you're
gonna do about dinner.


00:21:29.355 --> 00:21:32.665
Well, we'll be fine. We've actually
just pulled up to the pie shop.


00:21:33.826 --> 00:21:35.561
You gonna have pie for dinner?


00:21:35.562 --> 00:21:38.463
No. We're not gonna have pie for dinner.
We're gonna have macaroni for dinner.


00:21:38.464 --> 00:21:41.911
We have leftover macaroni.
We'll put that on top of the pie.


00:21:42.835 --> 00:21:44.370
All right.


00:21:44.571 --> 00:21:45.938
Will you get me the cherry-rhubarb?


00:21:45.939 --> 00:21:49.818
Cherry-rhubarb, got it. No problem.
Done. Love you. Bye.


00:21:49.876 --> 00:21:51.582
And ice cream.


00:21:52.512 --> 00:21:54.746
- What kind of ice cream?
- Chocolate.


00:21:54.747 --> 00:21:57.749
- On your macaroni?
- Ew! Not macaroni!


00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:59.518
It may be the grossest
thing I've ever heard.


00:21:59.519 --> 00:22:01.498
It's going to be an awesome dinner.


00:22:12.198 --> 00:22:14.833
Hey, Linda, you know what? You're lucky
that a 9-year-old makes the menu


00:22:14.834 --> 00:22:18.042
because that one in there
wants a macaroni pie.


00:22:51.037 --> 00:22:53.380
They didn't have chocolate
ice cream. So...


00:22:54.107 --> 00:22:56.211
Cass?


00:22:58.878 --> 00:23:00.254
Cass!


00:23:06.452 --> 00:23:08.056
Cass!


00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:22.735
Cass!


00:23:29.275 --> 00:23:31.015
Cass!


00:23:41.154 --> 00:23:43.655
- Hey, Linda, did Cass back here?
- No?


00:23:43.656 --> 00:23:46.762
Is she... is she in the back? Can you
take a look for me, please, thank you?


00:23:48.161 --> 00:23:50.334
- Nothing?
- No.


00:23:53.933 --> 00:23:55.969
Cass!


00:23:57.503 --> 00:23:59.448
Cassandra!


00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:02.450
Cass!


00:24:05.478 --> 00:24:06.888
Cass!


00:24:13.920 --> 00:24:15.524
Cass!


00:24:31.471 --> 00:24:33.973
I have a plan.


00:24:36.309 --> 00:24:38.049
A few minutes.


00:24:38.511 --> 00:24:40.786
That's all you'll have together.


00:24:42.915 --> 00:24:44.917
Do I get to talk to him?


00:24:45.318 --> 00:24:46.853
Yes.


00:24:49.255 --> 00:24:51.490
Does my Dad get to talk to me?


00:24:51.491 --> 00:24:54.232
Yes, Cass he does.


00:24:54.894 --> 00:24:56.795
And we'll be listening.


00:24:56.796 --> 00:25:01.267
Of course, I was thinking
some kind of mic...


00:25:01.601 --> 00:25:03.580
hidden microphone.


00:25:05.938 --> 00:25:08.111
What are you so worried about?


00:25:09.308 --> 00:25:11.685
I have no idea where I am.


00:25:12.612 --> 00:25:15.786
How would he ever find me?
I don't even know your name.


00:25:20.453 --> 00:25:22.694
Not a word...


00:25:24.190 --> 00:25:25.668
or else...


00:25:25.691 --> 00:25:27.534
You'll kill him.


00:25:33.499 --> 00:25:38.948
Wouldn't it just be easier to kill me...


00:25:42.442 --> 00:25:44.819
now that I'm all grown up?


00:25:46.946 --> 00:25:51.724
Now that you've lost interest.


00:25:54.353 --> 00:25:57.527
I can't be that valuable
doing what I'm doing.


00:26:01.594 --> 00:26:04.506
Oh, you are so valuable, Cassandra.


00:26:07.266 --> 00:26:11.043
Doing exactly what you're doing.


00:26:16.576 --> 00:26:20.614
- So it was the patrolman that flagged him?
- Yeah. Kicked down to us.


00:26:21.280 --> 00:26:23.282
- Okay.
- Ready?


00:26:23.382 --> 00:26:24.622
Yeah.


00:26:24.851 --> 00:26:27.729
- Okay?
- It's strange they'd send him here.


00:26:28.054 --> 00:26:30.489
Well, there weren't any
detectives at the main station.


00:26:30.490 --> 00:26:33.470
My buddy must have known
that I could do it.


00:26:34.827 --> 00:26:37.398
I'm not used to interviewing adults.


00:26:38.231 --> 00:26:39.801
You'll be fine.


00:26:41.934 --> 00:26:43.068
Mr. Lane.


00:26:43.069 --> 00:26:46.671
Hi. I'm Detective Dunlop and
this is Detective Cornwall.


00:26:46.672 --> 00:26:50.075
We have read through your statement that
you gave to the patrolman an hour ago.


00:26:50.076 --> 00:26:51.676
We'd just like to go over
a few details with you.


00:26:51.677 --> 00:26:53.019
Yeah. Good.


00:26:55.915 --> 00:26:57.449
Is it okay if we record this?


00:26:57.450 --> 00:27:00.089
Yeah. Did you see my wife?
Did someone give her a ride down?


00:27:00.520 --> 00:27:02.921
I don't know anything
about your wife, Mr. Lane.


00:27:02.922 --> 00:27:06.458
I... I called her three hours ago.
It shouldn't take her this long to get here.


00:27:06.459 --> 00:27:09.160
I'm worried that she went to the
main police station, not this one.


00:27:09.161 --> 00:27:10.969
I told her to take a cab.


00:27:11.330 --> 00:27:15.300
Okay. Let's just get
through these questions first


00:27:15.301 --> 00:27:17.435
and then we'll look into the
whereabouts of your wife. All right?


00:27:17.436 --> 00:27:21.509
Just to be clear, this conversation
is completely voluntary.


00:27:21.541 --> 00:27:24.609
And you are not being
forced to tell us anything.


00:27:24.610 --> 00:27:26.054
Do you understand this?


00:27:27.747 --> 00:27:29.481
- "Yes."
- Yes.


00:27:29.482 --> 00:27:34.619
Okay. Now, you say you were
in the diner for how long?


00:27:34.620 --> 00:27:37.289
A few minutes. Less.


00:27:37.290 --> 00:27:39.591
Okay. Were there any other customers?


00:27:39.592 --> 00:27:43.301
- No. I... I didn't see any.
- No customers.


00:27:43.496 --> 00:27:45.202
It says here you bought a pie?


00:27:45.798 --> 00:27:49.074
Yeah, we bought a...
we bought a cherry pie. My...


00:27:49.468 --> 00:27:51.570
my daughter... Yeah, we do
it every week after practice.


00:27:51.571 --> 00:27:52.704
I gotta get a pie.


00:27:52.705 --> 00:27:54.472
And I asked Linda if they
had chocolate ice cream...


00:27:54.473 --> 00:27:55.473
Sorry, you mean Lesley?


00:27:55.474 --> 00:27:57.453
And they... they... No.


00:27:57.543 --> 00:28:00.612
Linda. They didn't have any chocolate
ice cream. Can I call my wife now?


00:28:00.613 --> 00:28:03.286
It's "Lesley". I'm sorry,
it says Lesley right there.


00:28:04.450 --> 00:28:06.518
It says "Linda". I can see it from here.


00:28:06.519 --> 00:28:09.192
And my nine-year-old
daughter's another mile away.


00:28:09.555 --> 00:28:11.489
You have very good eyesight, Mr. Lane.


00:28:11.490 --> 00:28:13.692
But you claim you didn't see anything


00:28:13.693 --> 00:28:16.394
suspicious when you
looked back to the truck?


00:28:16.395 --> 00:28:18.602
It's been three hours since...


00:28:20.499 --> 00:28:23.868
someone driving, even if
he's going the speed limit,


00:28:23.869 --> 00:28:25.470
which he's not because
he's a fucking kidnapper,


00:28:25.471 --> 00:28:27.939
they're hundreds of miles away. Okay?


00:28:27.940 --> 00:28:28.974
They... they've taken my daughter.


00:28:28.975 --> 00:28:31.176
I need to know right now,
what are you doing to help?


00:28:31.177 --> 00:28:33.545
Have you got a helicopter up there?
Are you setting up a roadblock?


00:28:33.546 --> 00:28:35.180
What are you doing?
She's a ten-year-old girl.


00:28:35.181 --> 00:28:36.887
You said she was nine.


00:28:36.916 --> 00:28:38.190
What?


00:28:38.651 --> 00:28:41.519
You said she was nine.
Is she nine? Is she ten?


00:28:41.520 --> 00:28:43.221
What... what is she?


00:28:43.222 --> 00:28:46.100
She's almost ten. Christ,
what difference does it make?


00:28:46.892 --> 00:28:48.700
What difference does it...?


00:28:49.962 --> 00:28:52.942
- What's going on here?
- Linda... told the police


00:28:53.232 --> 00:28:56.611
that she never saw your daughter.


00:28:56.736 --> 00:28:59.341
Okay, so, what does that mean?


00:28:59.572 --> 00:29:03.053
When you pulled into the diner,
you were alone.


00:29:05.978 --> 00:29:07.379
Bullshit. I wasn't alone.


00:29:07.380 --> 00:29:09.748
She was resting in the back.
That's why she didn't see her.


00:29:09.749 --> 00:29:12.717
Okay. Why would she be resting
in the middle of the afternoon?


00:29:12.718 --> 00:29:15.053
Why wouldn't she be resting in the
middle of the fucking afternoon?


00:29:15.054 --> 00:29:19.557
She's a kid! A little girl, okay?
We just finished ice skating practice.


00:29:19.558 --> 00:29:21.459
- She was exhausted.
- Did you make any stops


00:29:21.460 --> 00:29:24.907
- between the rink and the diner?
- Okay.


00:29:26.432 --> 00:29:28.309
I'm gonna stop you right there.


00:29:30.069 --> 00:29:32.537
I was the last person to see
my daughter at the diner.


00:29:32.538 --> 00:29:34.711
That was me. Okay?


00:29:34.740 --> 00:29:38.476
Now, I would... I would like to
speak to somebody in charge.


00:29:38.477 --> 00:29:40.879
I'd like to speak to... to real police.


00:29:40.880 --> 00:29:44.349
I don't even... This looks like a
fucking kindergarten in here, okay.


00:29:44.350 --> 00:29:46.591
I need you to find my daughter, now!


00:29:50.790 --> 00:29:52.894
Mr. Lane, I'll ask again.


00:29:53.626 --> 00:29:58.103
Did you make any stops before
you arrived at the diner?


00:30:56.422 --> 00:30:58.731
I remember the day


00:30:59.492 --> 00:31:02.029
we won the trophy.


00:31:03.496 --> 00:31:08.741
The look on my mother's face as I
skated over and handed it to her.


00:31:10.569 --> 00:31:14.744
And it must be such an amazing
feeling for a parent,


00:31:15.741 --> 00:31:18.778
seeing their child realize a dream.


00:31:24.850 --> 00:31:28.388
That must be the hardest
part for Mum now,


00:31:30.656 --> 00:31:32.863
not knowing


00:31:33.659 --> 00:31:35.934
what I'm dreaming about.


00:31:37.463 --> 00:31:42.002
Or that I'm even alive to be dreaming.


00:31:46.872 --> 00:31:48.506
That's great, Cassandra.


00:31:48.507 --> 00:31:52.978
This time, do it again,
but a little less self-pity.


00:31:53.512 --> 00:31:56.314
Okay, do it, just one more
time and a little louder.


00:31:56.315 --> 00:31:59.056
Less self-pity. Got it?


00:32:16.402 --> 00:32:17.937
Tina...


00:32:18.370 --> 00:32:19.940
Tina.


00:32:20.139 --> 00:32:22.346
Tina, we stopped to get a pie.


00:32:22.474 --> 00:32:25.250
We stopped at the diner. You remember,
we spoke on the phone, remember?


00:32:25.344 --> 00:32:26.811
You remember, we stopped.
I got out of my truck.


00:32:26.812 --> 00:32:29.514
Right after we hung up I got out of
my truck and I went inside and I...


00:32:29.515 --> 00:32:31.983
I could see it. I could see it right
through the window. It was right there.


00:32:31.984 --> 00:32:34.252
The truck was right there and... and...


00:32:34.253 --> 00:32:36.554
And I went to the bathroom
for like two seconds


00:32:36.555 --> 00:32:39.160
and I came back out and
she was gone and she...


00:32:40.459 --> 00:32:43.963
What did you do? You lost our girl!


00:32:44.430 --> 00:32:46.598
You lost our girl!


00:32:46.599 --> 00:32:47.799
Don't.


00:32:47.800 --> 00:32:52.009
- No... No.
- She's gone...


00:33:06.118 --> 00:33:07.790
Mrs. Lane.


00:33:11.190 --> 00:33:14.701
- Mr. Lane, we need to speak to your wife now.
- It's gonna be okay.


00:33:14.860 --> 00:33:17.033
It's gonna be okay.


00:33:18.497 --> 00:33:21.102
Mrs. Lane.


00:33:23.502 --> 00:33:25.703
My name is Detective Dunlop.
I've been assigned to your case.


00:33:25.704 --> 00:33:28.150
- I just need to ask you a few questions.
- How long do you need to speak to her for?


00:33:28.507 --> 00:33:30.213
- A few minutes. Okay.
- Okay.


00:33:35.014 --> 00:33:36.549
Right here.


00:33:52.264 --> 00:33:55.802
I can't imagine what's going through
your wife's head right now.


00:33:57.536 --> 00:34:00.915
It's gotta be tough on you.
It's gotta be.


00:34:01.707 --> 00:34:05.882
Hey, listen, things get
crazy sometimes, you know?


00:34:08.347 --> 00:34:12.350
There seems to be some inconsistencies
about what your husband told us.


00:34:12.351 --> 00:34:16.321
Listen, I'm just... I'm going through the
files there, and I see... it's my job,


00:34:17.423 --> 00:34:19.960
I see you got an assault charge?


00:34:20.559 --> 00:34:22.129
Is that right?


00:34:25.698 --> 00:34:29.873
Teenage daddies with baby girls
shouldn't get into barroom brawls.


00:34:30.135 --> 00:34:31.536
Especially if they're not
old enough to drink.


00:34:31.537 --> 00:34:32.837
My wife knows about that.


00:34:32.838 --> 00:34:34.739
I was eighteen years old.
The fight was over her.


00:34:34.740 --> 00:34:38.983
So what, you quit school, you got a job
and now nine years later, you're broke.


00:34:40.212 --> 00:34:42.191
Yeah, money's tight. I get it.


00:34:45.451 --> 00:34:47.518
I heard you say something
to your wife about a...


00:34:47.519 --> 00:34:49.327
about a phone call.


00:34:49.388 --> 00:34:50.958
She called you, right?


00:34:51.056 --> 00:34:52.557
You didn't tell us about that.


00:34:52.558 --> 00:34:54.935
My partner's asking her
about that right now.


00:34:55.361 --> 00:34:57.862
Wondering if she spoke to
your daughter at that time.


00:34:57.863 --> 00:34:59.706
I guess if she didn't...


00:35:00.232 --> 00:35:02.100
if she didn't, then where is she?


00:35:02.101 --> 00:35:05.536
She's laying down in the back of the cab.
That's what she does. It's her little space.


00:35:05.537 --> 00:35:08.906
But don't kids stop taking afternoon naps
when they're like three or four years old?


00:35:08.907 --> 00:35:12.081
I mean, if my dad's buying my
favourite pie, I'm with him. I'm excited.


00:35:12.111 --> 00:35:14.648
Or I'm watching from the
car window, at least.


00:35:15.114 --> 00:35:16.991
Your business failed, right?


00:35:17.716 --> 00:35:19.417
Was it TM Landscaping?


00:35:19.418 --> 00:35:21.452
You got bills piling up.
You're about to go into bankruptcy.


00:35:21.453 --> 00:35:24.622
Like I said before, I get it.
I do, I get it.


00:35:24.623 --> 00:35:26.157
What the fuck are you talking about?


00:35:26.158 --> 00:35:28.424
Big money for lending your
daughter to some demented pal


00:35:28.525 --> 00:35:30.028
for a few days.
Then she's gonna show up,


00:35:30.029 --> 00:35:32.531
- damaged, but otherwise...
- You sick fucker!


00:35:38.170 --> 00:35:40.377
Excuse me, I'll be right back.


00:35:50.649 --> 00:35:53.651
This is what I do, okay? I give a
little shake, I see what falls out.


00:35:53.652 --> 00:35:56.387
As well, as give the judge every
reason to dismiss this case.


00:35:56.388 --> 00:35:58.489
He's not as innocent as he seems.


00:35:58.490 --> 00:36:00.758
- Maybe he is.
- He's got a criminal record.


00:36:00.759 --> 00:36:03.461
Assault. As well as a motive.
He owes money through his ears.


00:36:03.462 --> 00:36:07.498
So he creates an opportunity,
driving alone on a deserted highway.


00:36:07.499 --> 00:36:09.000
Give me a break.


00:36:09.101 --> 00:36:10.511
Hey!


00:36:15.374 --> 00:36:17.108
He reminds me of someone.


00:36:17.109 --> 00:36:18.883
Somebody from your past.


00:36:19.812 --> 00:36:21.655
Yeah, from my past.


00:36:22.514 --> 00:36:24.288
This is the present.


00:36:31.457 --> 00:36:35.427
Do you actually believe any of the things
he said to Matt the night we came in?


00:36:37.930 --> 00:36:41.206
I'm not going to excuse the way
that he behaved with Matthew.


00:36:41.667 --> 00:36:44.068
He's dealt with a lot of cases
where someone from the family,


00:36:44.069 --> 00:36:46.913
even a parent, is involved.


00:36:47.706 --> 00:36:50.015
Matthew reminded him of someone.


00:36:51.076 --> 00:36:54.386
- Someone personal.
- That's just bullshit.


00:36:56.548 --> 00:36:59.654
Matthew loved Cassandra more
than anything in this world.


00:37:00.752 --> 00:37:02.663
He still loves her.


00:37:03.956 --> 00:37:05.491
Of course.


00:37:05.791 --> 00:37:08.498
I don't know if I want
to do this anymore.


00:37:09.461 --> 00:37:11.099
I understand. It's up to you.


00:37:11.230 --> 00:37:13.266
Happy to meet you when you need.


00:37:37.589 --> 00:37:41.662
On this pillow you will find...


00:37:44.263 --> 00:37:48.404
a teeny-tiny tooth of mine.


00:37:53.238 --> 00:37:57.752
So while I sleep, where dreams are made


00:37:58.410 --> 00:38:01.254
let's see if we can make this trade.


00:38:10.789 --> 00:38:14.293
Money for teeth.


00:38:18.096 --> 00:38:22.100
It just seems strange to
exchange them for money.


00:38:22.935 --> 00:38:26.211
But it's something we all do.


00:38:28.440 --> 00:38:29.975
Or did.


00:38:33.745 --> 00:38:39.058
And if there ever was a Tooth
Fairy that visited me here,


00:38:40.719 --> 00:38:45.929
I'm sure there's something more useful
she could do than leaving me a dollar.


00:38:48.427 --> 00:38:51.032
Or maybe it's just a trick.


00:38:58.337 --> 00:39:02.944
A trick or a gimmick.


00:39:04.810 --> 00:39:07.620
A gimmick you don't really need.


00:39:08.680 --> 00:39:11.592
Yes, that's the proper word.


00:39:52.057 --> 00:39:54.059
Tina...


00:40:02.067 --> 00:40:03.409
How are you?


00:40:04.636 --> 00:40:06.843
I'm fine, I guess.


00:40:08.674 --> 00:40:11.882
Hard to believe I've been coming
to see you for six years.


00:40:13.712 --> 00:40:17.415
You look really good.
Better than last time.


00:40:17.416 --> 00:40:19.623
Yeah, I was a mess last time.


00:40:25.590 --> 00:40:27.228
How's Matthew?


00:40:29.428 --> 00:40:31.464
He's fine.


00:40:31.596 --> 00:40:34.167
Can I ask what's happening?


00:40:34.299 --> 00:40:36.005
I still can't look at him.


00:40:36.468 --> 00:40:37.878
I see Cass.


00:40:38.036 --> 00:40:41.244
I get mad. I say awful things.


00:40:42.074 --> 00:40:43.507
Is he completely out of the picture?


00:40:43.508 --> 00:40:45.282
- Last time...
- No.


00:40:45.477 --> 00:40:48.355
I was just speaking to him, actually.
He said that...


00:40:48.880 --> 00:40:50.791
that he wanted to come here.


00:40:51.350 --> 00:40:53.056
So why didn't he?


00:40:53.819 --> 00:40:55.853
I called him and left him a message.


00:40:55.854 --> 00:40:58.163
He thought I'd end up screaming at him.


00:40:59.791 --> 00:41:01.429
Would you?


00:41:01.960 --> 00:41:03.495
Probably.


00:41:06.098 --> 00:41:08.942
He still thinks he's gonna
find her on his own.


00:41:09.101 --> 00:41:11.080
Does he tell you how?


00:41:11.903 --> 00:41:13.704
You mean does he have a plan?


00:41:13.705 --> 00:41:15.445
Matthew?


00:41:15.874 --> 00:41:18.075
Oh yeah. His plan is that
he's on the road a lot.


00:41:18.076 --> 00:41:20.078
He keeps his eyes open. Idiot.


00:41:23.081 --> 00:41:25.492
I don't sound very nice, do I?


00:41:25.717 --> 00:41:27.451
I've heard a lot worse.


00:41:27.452 --> 00:41:29.056
Yeah, I bet.


00:41:30.956 --> 00:41:33.026
I couldn't do what you do.


00:41:41.099 --> 00:41:42.533
You have a daughter?


00:41:42.534 --> 00:41:43.910
No.


00:41:49.274 --> 00:41:52.687
That's Jeffrey's niece, Jennifer.


00:41:53.612 --> 00:41:56.456
- They're really close.
- That's nice.


00:41:58.517 --> 00:42:01.190
So should we start?


00:42:08.693 --> 00:42:11.935
When you think of Cass,


00:42:13.231 --> 00:42:15.074
what do you see?


00:42:17.602 --> 00:42:19.172
What do I see?


00:42:21.540 --> 00:42:24.816
Mostly I think about her skating.
She loved it so much.


00:42:25.544 --> 00:42:27.912
She and Albert,
that was her partner, they...


00:42:27.913 --> 00:42:30.147
they talked about going to the Olympics.


00:42:30.148 --> 00:42:33.584
And Matt still goes to the rink sometimes
just to watch Albert practice.


00:42:33.585 --> 00:42:36.691
It's like they're both just
waiting for Cass to come back.


00:42:37.522 --> 00:42:39.899
And Albert's really strong.


00:42:39.991 --> 00:42:43.904
So if Cass stays small like me...


00:42:45.130 --> 00:42:47.803
They could carry on where they left off.


00:42:54.473 --> 00:42:55.951
We're here.


00:43:02.414 --> 00:43:03.747
Mrs. Lane.


00:43:03.748 --> 00:43:05.056
Hi.


00:43:05.250 --> 00:43:06.990
Hello.


00:43:07.986 --> 00:43:09.396
Come in.


00:43:14.593 --> 00:43:16.037
Please.


00:43:21.099 --> 00:43:22.771
Okay.


00:43:24.503 --> 00:43:26.737
Mrs. Lane, do you know a
lot of illegal images of kids


00:43:26.738 --> 00:43:29.047
are circulated on the internet?


00:43:30.575 --> 00:43:34.613
And any picture like that is actual
evidence of where a crime has taken place.


00:43:34.880 --> 00:43:36.620
Do you understand that?


00:43:36.982 --> 00:43:38.716
We study these crime scene images.


00:43:38.717 --> 00:43:41.118
We use whatever information
we get out of them to track


00:43:41.119 --> 00:43:43.554
down the people who trade
in these illegal pictures.


00:43:43.555 --> 00:43:47.730
To find the children. To rescue them.


00:43:48.059 --> 00:43:51.039
Sometimes to gain access
to certain rooms,


00:43:52.797 --> 00:43:54.571
I play a role.


00:43:58.436 --> 00:44:01.177
I try and fit in with the
other men who are...


00:44:01.439 --> 00:44:06.183
who are watching the abuse
that's taking place in a room.


00:44:06.211 --> 00:44:10.158
The men are all connected to a camera.


00:44:10.682 --> 00:44:15.892
They might give directions
or participate.


00:44:17.322 --> 00:44:21.964
- A live camera that's in a room.
- Doing what?


00:44:24.029 --> 00:44:25.974
Watching a child.


00:44:29.734 --> 00:44:34.182
Jeffrey believes that he may


00:44:34.739 --> 00:44:37.014
have found some images of Cass.


00:44:38.577 --> 00:44:41.078
- You found her?
- No. No, no, no. Just a...


00:44:41.079 --> 00:44:45.015
a few screen grabs. Pictures. That's it.


00:44:45.016 --> 00:44:47.257
They were recent.


00:44:47.719 --> 00:44:50.062
So the good...


00:44:50.155 --> 00:44:53.568
- the really good news...
- She's alive.


00:45:51.583 --> 00:45:53.118
Mrs. Lane?


00:46:00.659 --> 00:46:02.536
Tina?


00:46:04.396 --> 00:46:07.001
Do you think this could be Cass?


00:46:11.336 --> 00:46:13.144
I think so.


00:46:38.530 --> 00:46:40.202
Hey... How'd it go?


00:46:40.265 --> 00:46:43.075
Matthew, listen to me.
They showed me a picture of her.


00:46:43.401 --> 00:46:45.744
They found a picture of her.


00:46:47.072 --> 00:46:49.051
What do you mean, a picture of Cass?


00:46:50.275 --> 00:46:51.617
From where?


00:46:52.544 --> 00:46:55.081
They don't know.
They found it on a computer.


00:46:57.215 --> 00:46:59.583
Well, when was...
when was the picture from?


00:46:59.584 --> 00:47:01.518
They don't know. It was just her face.


00:47:01.519 --> 00:47:05.660
They just showed me a picture of her face.
But it's... it's her, Matthew, it's her.


00:47:06.891 --> 00:47:08.893
What's she doing in the photo?


00:47:08.960 --> 00:47:10.336
Well...


00:47:10.562 --> 00:47:11.595
Tina?


00:47:11.596 --> 00:47:14.631
Like I said, they... they don't know.
You know, it was just her face. But...


00:47:14.632 --> 00:47:17.034
but they said that she was
talking to another girl.


00:47:17.035 --> 00:47:18.435
Like a younger girl.


00:47:18.436 --> 00:47:19.937
Okay, but... okay. Okay, I got it.


00:47:19.938 --> 00:47:23.544
But, what... what's she actually
doing in the... in the picture?


00:47:23.708 --> 00:47:25.881
Like, I said, they don't know. Like...


00:47:26.411 --> 00:47:28.946
You could have been there and then
you would know all of this already.


00:47:28.947 --> 00:47:30.414
I said they don't know.


00:47:30.415 --> 00:47:31.825
Okay?


00:47:32.417 --> 00:47:36.455
But it was her. It was
her face. And they said...


00:47:37.021 --> 00:47:38.966
they said that... you know,


00:47:39.290 --> 00:47:42.559
they're always looking for children
and that Cass is like a...


00:47:42.560 --> 00:47:44.971
I can't remember exactly what they said.


00:47:45.697 --> 00:47:49.269
But they said she's like a...
like a welcoming face on a gateway.


00:47:49.534 --> 00:47:51.741
Or... or something like that.


00:47:51.903 --> 00:47:54.041
Gateway? What do you mean a gateway?


00:47:54.906 --> 00:47:56.714
To what?


00:48:06.551 --> 00:48:08.428
Tina?


00:48:10.655 --> 00:48:13.135
To a ring, they said.


00:48:15.994 --> 00:48:20.806
Welcoming face to a gateway, to a ring.


00:48:23.134 --> 00:48:27.437
She's helping lure other kids...


00:48:27.438 --> 00:48:29.042
Honey...


00:48:29.874 --> 00:48:32.047
They've made her like them.


00:48:35.413 --> 00:48:37.950
That's what happened to
our daughter, Matthew.


00:48:41.252 --> 00:48:43.925
She's helping recruit other kids.


00:48:45.824 --> 00:48:49.168
That's what happened
when you left her alone.


00:48:50.695 --> 00:48:53.402
Those monsters came and took her.


00:48:53.431 --> 00:48:55.911
And now she sits with her smiling face


00:48:56.301 --> 00:48:58.144
and talks to other babies.


00:48:59.070 --> 00:49:01.379
And then they go and get them.


00:49:02.740 --> 00:49:10.988
That's what happened to her
when you left her alone.


00:49:22.193 --> 00:49:25.674
My fate is grief and lamentation.


00:49:27.232 --> 00:49:30.269
My daughter's life has been betrayed.


00:49:31.336 --> 00:49:34.339
All joy has turned to desolation.


00:49:34.572 --> 00:49:37.609
An evil friend has stolen her away.


00:49:41.946 --> 00:49:44.084
Is that how you see yourself...


00:49:44.949 --> 00:49:46.894
as an evil friend?


00:49:47.619 --> 00:49:49.496
Sometimes.


00:49:51.122 --> 00:49:53.101
Where is this from?


00:49:54.592 --> 00:49:57.436
Mozart. It's the...


00:49:58.062 --> 00:50:01.907
Queen of the Night's aria
from The Magic Flute.


00:50:02.267 --> 00:50:04.804
And how's it going to
help you catch any kids?


00:50:05.937 --> 00:50:07.304
What do you mean?


00:50:07.305 --> 00:50:10.581
It doesn't seem like the sort of
thing that would attract them.


00:50:12.543 --> 00:50:14.181
It's not.


00:50:19.584 --> 00:50:21.927
It's part of story time, Cass.


00:50:23.187 --> 00:50:25.132
But it's not my story.


00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:43.645
The only thing I have to do today


00:50:44.742 --> 00:50:47.744
Is to get to the garden


00:50:47.745 --> 00:50:50.314
To pick some sage


00:50:50.315 --> 00:50:56.993
And wrap lavender with blue string


00:50:58.122 --> 00:51:03.731
And set the cedar leaves out for drying


00:51:10.435 --> 00:51:12.937
Is it spring yet?


00:51:16.374 --> 00:51:17.511
No.


00:51:18.176 --> 00:51:20.587
What's happening with my Dad?


00:51:21.312 --> 00:51:23.052
You promised.


00:51:29.153 --> 00:51:30.893
Why don't you just...


00:51:32.490 --> 00:51:37.029
get back to reading
about your evil friend?


00:51:44.502 --> 00:51:50.179
I still see her shaking,
her heart breaking.


00:51:51.342 --> 00:51:55.881
How dreadful her crying,
how hopeless her sighing...


00:52:45.263 --> 00:52:46.663
Make her ears stick out.


00:52:46.664 --> 00:52:48.609
- Why?
- It's hotter.


00:52:49.267 --> 00:52:51.701
- Pardon me?
- Well, if you're going to bait the trap...


00:52:51.702 --> 00:52:53.909
Use the best bait.


00:52:56.507 --> 00:52:59.810
If you're going for hot,
cross your eyes a little.


00:52:59.811 --> 00:53:01.881
What? It's true. Try it.


00:53:03.147 --> 00:53:04.682
That's weird, man.


00:53:05.450 --> 00:53:08.897
- The cross eyes are perfect.
- All right.


00:53:12.156 --> 00:53:12.989
We're on.


00:53:12.990 --> 00:53:15.128
- Is it Willy?
- Yeah, Willy.


00:53:25.369 --> 00:53:28.509
Reel him in, Jeff. Reel him in.


00:53:29.373 --> 00:53:32.046
Come on, come on, come on, come on.


00:53:34.145 --> 00:53:36.090
Yes! Yes!


00:54:17.989 --> 00:54:19.160
Hi.


00:54:19.624 --> 00:54:21.125
It's Willy.


00:54:24.595 --> 00:54:26.301
Sorry. My mistake.


00:54:26.531 --> 00:54:28.135
You bet it is.


00:54:28.933 --> 00:54:32.004
Stop! Stop right there!


00:54:32.837 --> 00:54:34.941
It's not what you think!
I'm a Good Samaritan.


00:54:34.972 --> 00:54:38.542
Well, these arrests are the
result of amazing team work.


00:54:38.543 --> 00:54:41.511
Incredible cooperation from a
number of different departments.


00:54:41.512 --> 00:54:44.581
- Next time you're doing this.
- You look good on camera.


00:54:44.582 --> 00:54:46.789
...the public and media.


00:54:47.418 --> 00:54:51.024
You know, we all have to be vigilant.


00:54:51.222 --> 00:54:54.566
You know, there may be young people
who are watching this right now,


00:54:54.825 --> 00:54:57.794
some of you might have come to see me.


00:54:57.795 --> 00:55:00.605
And you've trusted me with your stories


00:55:00.731 --> 00:55:03.700
- and I want you to remember...
- I see you do that, you know.


00:55:03.701 --> 00:55:07.182
When you're in that room
with those kids, I watch you.


00:55:07.772 --> 00:55:09.739
The way you get them
to trust you like that.


00:55:09.740 --> 00:55:12.015
The way you talk to them. It's amazing.


00:55:13.211 --> 00:55:14.815
Look at me.


00:55:15.112 --> 00:55:17.216
No, look at me. You're amazing.


00:55:17.615 --> 00:55:20.288
- You're amazing.
- ...we'll show them that we can win.


00:55:20.384 --> 00:55:22.018
So, you know,


00:55:22.019 --> 00:55:23.920
- Thank you.
- If you're a young person out there


00:55:23.921 --> 00:55:26.022
and you think that an adult around you


00:55:26.023 --> 00:55:28.503
is behaving or acting in
an inappropriate way...


00:55:28.559 --> 00:55:29.993
I want you to call us.


00:55:29.994 --> 00:55:32.804
Call the police. We are here to help.


00:55:32.930 --> 00:55:34.831
And... and also, you know, if...


00:55:34.832 --> 00:55:38.301
if you are online and you
meet any stranger online,


00:55:38.302 --> 00:55:41.942
be very careful,
in any chat or in any way,


00:55:42.373 --> 00:55:44.250
you have to be on guard.


00:55:47.311 --> 00:55:50.883
I know that it'll... it'll all work out.


00:55:55.753 --> 00:55:58.028
What makes you so sure?


00:56:00.391 --> 00:56:05.704
They have only cracked the first ring.


00:56:07.531 --> 00:56:10.978
They'll never get to us. We are safe.


00:56:11.202 --> 00:56:14.342
Encrypted beyond the reach of God.


00:56:16.774 --> 00:56:19.379
Do not give them the key, Willy.


00:56:19.710 --> 00:56:22.486
Under no circumstance do you


00:56:22.747 --> 00:56:25.715
take any of the bullshit
deals that they offer.


00:56:25.716 --> 00:56:28.918
You deny. Deny, deny, deny, deny, deny.


00:56:28.919 --> 00:56:34.425
That bitch that set me up,
I want her removed.


00:56:36.560 --> 00:56:39.165
- She's a cop, Willy.
- I don't care.


00:56:39.730 --> 00:56:41.766
That's what I want.


00:56:43.067 --> 00:56:44.668
- Willy, just listen to me for a second...
- No.


00:56:44.669 --> 00:56:46.944
- No. No!
- That's not...


00:56:47.104 --> 00:56:50.983
You listen to me, cousin.


00:56:52.276 --> 00:56:55.848
I'll keep quiet about our little club


00:56:55.880 --> 00:56:58.815
as long as she's taught a lesson.


00:56:58.816 --> 00:57:02.320
I... I want her buried.


00:57:03.454 --> 00:57:05.126
Like the others.


00:57:05.656 --> 00:57:08.158
Only she stays alive.


00:57:10.494 --> 00:57:13.804
She tells me her stories.


00:57:14.532 --> 00:57:17.672
All of her stories.


00:57:22.773 --> 00:57:25.378
I lost this one yesterday.


00:57:25.409 --> 00:57:27.149
You know what the best idea is?


00:57:27.478 --> 00:57:30.180
Write a note beside your tooth
when you put it under your pillow.


00:57:30.181 --> 00:57:32.854
That way the Tooth Fairy will
know what to get you next time.


00:57:32.917 --> 00:57:35.151
But letters are for Santa.


00:57:35.152 --> 00:57:37.427
Do you still believe in Santa?


00:57:37.588 --> 00:57:39.294
Sometimes.


00:57:40.591 --> 00:57:42.570
Okay. Well, I'm not
talking about a letter.


00:57:42.593 --> 00:57:44.094
Just a note.


00:57:44.829 --> 00:57:48.208
If you want we can meet and I
can show you how to write one.


00:57:48.499 --> 00:57:50.774
That way you can get anything you want.


00:57:53.504 --> 00:57:55.438
I thought you weren't coming 'til later?


00:57:55.439 --> 00:57:56.373
What's going on?


00:57:56.374 --> 00:57:58.608
Look. Look. Don't let
this freak you out, okay?


00:57:58.609 --> 00:58:00.076
I talked to my brother.
He knows everything.


00:58:00.077 --> 00:58:02.147
He's cool. He's okay. It's okay.


00:58:02.179 --> 00:58:04.852
- What?
- Hey, hey, hey, She's talking to Cass.


00:58:04.949 --> 00:58:06.316
She's talking to Cass.


00:58:06.317 --> 00:58:08.194
Get Jennifer to find out where she is.


00:58:08.619 --> 00:58:11.065
Nicole. Nicole!


00:58:11.322 --> 00:58:13.859
- Nicole!
- Hi, Nicole. We're playing a game.


00:58:19.230 --> 00:58:20.970
What happened?


00:58:21.265 --> 00:58:23.005
I don't know.


00:58:23.634 --> 00:58:26.171
Hey, would you mind waiting
in the bedroom for a little bit?


00:58:27.037 --> 00:58:30.140
- We were just playing a game.
- No. I know. I understand.


00:58:30.141 --> 00:58:33.144
I just need to talk to your
uncle for a little bit, okay?


00:58:35.112 --> 00:58:38.615
- Did I do something wrong?
- No. No, you did nothing wrong.


00:58:38.616 --> 00:58:41.584
As a matter of fact, there's a
book back there waiting for you.


00:58:41.585 --> 00:58:43.987
The sequel to the one you asked for


00:58:43.988 --> 00:58:47.765
and I would love for you to get started
on that, tell me what you think.


00:59:02.573 --> 00:59:05.375
- Are you out of your mind?
- Do you have any idea what you just did?


00:59:05.376 --> 00:59:07.343
- Do you have any idea?
- You put Jennifer online.


00:59:07.344 --> 00:59:08.578
I'm in contact.


00:59:08.579 --> 00:59:10.413
I've been trying to break in forever!


00:59:10.414 --> 00:59:12.582
Okay, I needed to show I
had access to a real girl.


00:59:12.583 --> 00:59:15.654
- What?
- To get to Cass.


00:59:15.920 --> 00:59:19.333
That's what she does, okay?
She helps them bring them in.


00:59:20.224 --> 00:59:21.090
Nothing happened here.


00:59:21.091 --> 00:59:22.225
- Nothing!
- Nothing?


00:59:22.226 --> 00:59:23.693
- Nothing.
- ...except images of Cass.


00:59:23.694 --> 00:59:25.061
Images of nothing!


00:59:25.062 --> 00:59:27.397
Of her talking in this room.
That's it. That's all.


00:59:27.398 --> 00:59:30.606
You don't use children!


00:59:36.173 --> 00:59:38.041
- Listen to me.
- No, no, no, no, no.


00:59:38.042 --> 00:59:40.249
- Don't touch me.
- Listen to me.


00:59:40.511 --> 00:59:43.580
- I screwed up, okay? I screwed up.
- You're out of my unit.


00:59:43.581 --> 00:59:45.014
I should have done this a long time ago.


00:59:45.015 --> 00:59:46.816
Try to take it easy.
We got tonight, please.


00:59:46.817 --> 00:59:48.785
I don't want you there tonight.


00:59:48.786 --> 00:59:51.421
- You don't want me there tonight?
- No. I'm going alone.


00:59:51.422 --> 00:59:52.900
Okay, you're going alone.


00:59:53.390 --> 00:59:57.099
Jennifer, baby.
I gotta go, I'll call you soon.


01:00:38.035 --> 01:00:39.343
Detective Dunlop.


01:00:39.670 --> 01:00:40.904
Hi.


01:00:40.905 --> 01:00:42.639
- Nicole.
- Hi. Diane Grey.


01:00:42.640 --> 01:00:45.810
I'm so glad you could make it.
You look... just fabulous.


01:00:45.911 --> 01:00:48.115
- Thank you. You look beautiful.
- Thank you.


01:00:48.312 --> 01:00:51.190
Are you alone? I... I thought
you were coming with a guest.


01:00:51.582 --> 01:00:54.995
He had a work emergency.


01:00:55.052 --> 01:00:57.691
Of course. Please come in.


01:00:58.822 --> 01:01:01.424
Is there anything you want help
with this evening that I...?


01:01:01.425 --> 01:01:05.372
- I mean straightforward.
- Yeah, I just... no, no thank you...


01:01:05.429 --> 01:01:08.531
- I feel that I should've wrote something...
- Hello, gorgeous lady.


01:01:08.532 --> 01:01:11.535
- Mika! Very well.
 - How are you? You look lovely tonight.


01:01:11.536 --> 01:01:14.645
 Thank you. Let me introduce
you to Detective Dunlop.


01:01:32.790 --> 01:01:33.823
Thank you.


01:01:33.824 --> 01:01:35.962
Can I talk you into a
glass of champagne?


01:01:36.093 --> 01:01:37.594
Oh, no thank you.


01:01:37.595 --> 01:01:41.599
Detective Dunlop, I'm Vince Grey.


01:01:42.666 --> 01:01:44.270
Oh, Diane's Vince.


01:01:44.435 --> 01:01:47.971
Yeah. Yeah. This is...


01:01:47.972 --> 01:01:49.772
this is remarkable.


01:01:49.773 --> 01:01:53.277
I mean, the difference
really is... that's...


01:01:54.578 --> 01:01:56.879
Is this the way you dress at work?


01:01:56.880 --> 01:01:59.883
No. I do a lot of my work with children.


01:02:00.050 --> 01:02:02.552
- They wouldn't feel comfortable...
- Yeah, with that look of authority.


01:02:02.553 --> 01:02:04.794
I guess most of them
feel betrayed by that.


01:02:05.356 --> 01:02:08.860
- By what?
- By the people they're supposed to trust.


01:02:10.794 --> 01:02:12.932
Here you are.


01:02:13.063 --> 01:02:14.430
Sorry. I didn't mean to...


01:02:14.431 --> 01:02:15.732
Did I say something to...


01:02:15.733 --> 01:02:17.667
- You're on.
- Okay.


01:02:17.668 --> 01:02:18.701
Okay.


01:02:18.702 --> 01:02:21.045
- Excuse me. Nice to meet you too.
- Nice to meet you.


01:02:21.538 --> 01:02:22.305
Everything okay?


01:02:22.306 --> 01:02:23.539
Yeah. Good.


01:02:23.540 --> 01:02:25.475
My deepest thank you.


01:02:25.476 --> 01:02:28.878
Without your generosity, an evening
like this simply wouldn't happen.


01:02:28.879 --> 01:02:30.880
And we wouldn't be able to celebrate


01:02:30.881 --> 01:02:34.851
the remarkable woman I'm
about to introduce to you.


01:02:35.452 --> 01:02:39.856
Why Detective Nicole Dunlop has
become a very public figure recently,


01:02:39.857 --> 01:02:44.737
most of her time is spent in a
room where she listens to stories.


01:02:44.895 --> 01:02:51.471
Stories told by the most vulnerable
members of our society, our children.


01:02:51.735 --> 01:02:55.580
They come to trust her.
And they feel safe.


01:02:57.141 --> 01:02:59.709
The difference between a youth at risk


01:02:59.710 --> 01:03:04.886
and a young person with their
whole life ahead of them


01:03:05.749 --> 01:03:09.458
is care and concern.


01:03:11.555 --> 01:03:16.970
I know this because I nearly
fell through the cracks.


01:03:17.895 --> 01:03:19.999
I was living on the street.


01:03:20.064 --> 01:03:25.912
I spent my fourteenth birthday
sleeping in an abandoned van.


01:03:26.537 --> 01:03:29.813
If I hadn't been placed with
the right foster family,


01:03:29.907 --> 01:03:32.011
I'd have stayed there.


01:03:32.876 --> 01:03:34.980
And that's a scary thought.


01:03:36.213 --> 01:03:38.852
Because the kids I know from those days


01:03:40.050 --> 01:03:44.657
disappeared or died.


01:03:47.424 --> 01:03:50.268
If I showed you pictures
related to my work


01:03:50.994 --> 01:03:52.996
most of you would cry.


01:03:53.497 --> 01:03:59.276
The awful truth is that there are no
happy endings in my line of work.


01:03:59.503 --> 01:04:06.887
There are only stories that just stop.


01:04:11.115 --> 01:04:12.491
On a good day,


01:04:13.117 --> 01:04:15.528
I capture the scum of the earth.


01:04:15.753 --> 01:04:17.630
On a good day,


01:04:17.921 --> 01:04:21.561
I help a damaged young person


01:04:21.625 --> 01:04:23.626
take a step forward


01:04:23.627 --> 01:04:28.075
on a very long journey through
the kind of nightmare that


01:04:29.266 --> 01:04:31.803
would ruin this lovely dinner.


01:04:36.974 --> 01:04:38.612
Listen,


01:04:41.712 --> 01:04:44.192
you don't want me in your life.


01:04:46.450 --> 01:04:50.397
You never want me to
come into the picture.


01:04:51.955 --> 01:04:53.957
Not with your child.


01:04:55.025 --> 01:04:57.693
So please, write big cheques


01:04:57.694 --> 01:05:01.107
and maybe none of you will
ever have to see me again.


01:05:03.500 --> 01:05:06.776
It's been such an honour
to be here. Thank you.


01:05:15.078 --> 01:05:17.558
The speech is over.


01:05:17.748 --> 01:05:21.889
We broke all our records,
thanks to you. It is time to celebrate.


01:05:25.122 --> 01:05:27.295
- All right. One glass.
- Okay.


01:05:28.992 --> 01:05:30.560
Cheers. Thank you so much.


01:05:30.561 --> 01:05:32.528
- Cheers. Thank you.
- Cheers.


01:05:32.529 --> 01:05:34.770
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.


01:05:37.701 --> 01:05:40.369
So, I... I got to ask you,


01:05:40.370 --> 01:05:43.248
how can you stand to be in the same room


01:05:43.473 --> 01:05:45.452
as some of these people?


01:05:46.343 --> 01:05:48.584
Criminals are easy.


01:05:48.979 --> 01:05:51.550
The tough part is the technology.


01:05:51.715 --> 01:05:54.786
Really? How... how so?


01:05:56.520 --> 01:06:02.658
Well, right now we're working with
this locked network that has the best


01:06:02.659 --> 01:06:04.594
encryption we've ever seen.


01:06:04.595 --> 01:06:09.665
So, the bad guys are winning then?
Is that what you're saying?


01:06:09.666 --> 01:06:12.476
Well, my guys are really good.


01:06:13.904 --> 01:06:16.850
You know, my guys are really good and...
and one of them thinks that...


01:06:17.140 --> 01:06:18.516
Well...


01:06:21.545 --> 01:06:23.149
I'm sorry.


01:06:24.014 --> 01:06:27.518
I'm sorry that just got...
got past security.


01:06:28.552 --> 01:06:30.920
No, I'm sorry. Once you get me going...


01:06:30.921 --> 01:06:34.834
No, it's... No Mika and I are just...
we're working on a big project.


01:06:34.958 --> 01:06:40.339
The day after begins before
the day before ends. It's just.


01:06:41.732 --> 01:06:43.466
Oh, I can't even read that.


01:06:43.467 --> 01:06:44.500
Is it getting late?


01:06:44.501 --> 01:06:48.244
That's why they make women's watches
so small, so you can't see how late it is.


01:07:11.828 --> 01:07:13.170
Oh, that's great.


01:07:13.997 --> 01:07:16.670
- Now just pour me into a taxi.
- A taxi?


01:07:16.867 --> 01:07:18.812
No, why don't I give you a ride.


01:07:23.941 --> 01:07:25.647
Thank you.


01:07:31.014 --> 01:07:32.492
Thanks.


01:08:06.116 --> 01:08:07.984
I better call my boyfriend.


01:08:07.985 --> 01:08:11.120
- Why?
- 'Cause I don't feel very well.


01:08:11.121 --> 01:08:13.100
No, you look fine.


01:08:15.425 --> 01:08:17.560
I don't want him to worry.


01:08:17.561 --> 01:08:19.506
Well, let him worry.


01:08:20.197 --> 01:08:22.267
You're not a helpless child.


01:08:24.701 --> 01:08:26.509
Hey.


01:08:30.507 --> 01:08:31.951
Come here.


01:08:40.050 --> 01:08:43.831
You know, one professional to another,


01:08:44.654 --> 01:08:48.033
I wish I'd met someone like
you when I was a little girl.


01:09:56.259 --> 01:09:58.194
Are you joking?
Didn't you get the message?


01:09:58.195 --> 01:09:58.961
What message?


01:09:58.962 --> 01:10:01.197
There's a snowstorm out here.
I'm sending everybody home.


01:10:01.198 --> 01:10:03.299
Anyway, I want these here tomorrow
when the landscaper's here.


01:10:03.300 --> 01:10:04.600
Hey, I was driving all day man.


01:10:04.601 --> 01:10:06.502
- You can place them where they need to go...
- didn't plan on spending the night.


01:10:06.503 --> 01:10:08.904
Listen, there's a place
just down the highway.


01:10:08.905 --> 01:10:11.107
The Richard Lake Motel. Just stay there.


01:10:11.108 --> 01:10:13.849
Bring the receipts, I'll look after it.


01:14:06.609 --> 01:14:08.383
Hi, Daddy.


01:14:14.217 --> 01:14:15.991
No cry.


01:14:23.593 --> 01:14:25.538
Are you... are you okay?


01:14:26.463 --> 01:14:29.000
You okay? Yeah?


01:14:34.504 --> 01:14:37.041
Oh, I've missed you so much.


01:14:41.544 --> 01:14:44.388
- Hey, are you okay?
- I'm okay.


01:14:44.481 --> 01:14:46.892
- Yeah?
- How's Mum?


01:14:50.620 --> 01:14:52.599
We miss you so much


01:14:54.758 --> 01:14:57.966
I wanted to see you so much.


01:14:58.561 --> 01:15:02.065
He understood. Just this once.


01:15:02.499 --> 01:15:04.945
He wanted me to be happy.


01:15:05.535 --> 01:15:08.015
- As happy as I could be, so...
- Who?


01:15:08.538 --> 01:15:10.016
Who, Cass?


01:15:12.175 --> 01:15:13.619
Who?


01:15:14.944 --> 01:15:17.546
I thought... I've thought about
you every second of the day.


01:15:17.547 --> 01:15:19.715
- I'm so sorry. I should never have left you.
- There's nothing...


01:15:19.716 --> 01:15:21.450
I shouldn't have left you.


01:15:21.451 --> 01:15:23.123
No, you shouldn't have.


01:15:23.453 --> 01:15:25.354
But it happened so fast.


01:15:25.355 --> 01:15:28.233
They would have got me anyway.
They were following us.


01:15:29.459 --> 01:15:30.903
Who?


01:15:33.062 --> 01:15:34.973
Who, Cass, who are they?


01:15:35.064 --> 01:15:37.533
Come on. You gotta come home


01:15:37.534 --> 01:15:38.634
to Mum. Let's go.


01:15:38.635 --> 01:15:40.842
- Was it just a trick?
- Come on. What?


01:15:41.237 --> 01:15:42.943
The day you lost me.


01:15:43.039 --> 01:15:44.779
Was it just a trick?


01:15:45.241 --> 01:15:47.509
Or maybe gimmick's a better word.


01:15:47.510 --> 01:15:49.545
Something we didn't need.


01:15:49.546 --> 01:15:52.959
We were so good. We didn't need
anything like to get attention.


01:15:53.650 --> 01:15:55.350
What, Cass? What are you talking about?


01:15:55.351 --> 01:15:57.194
One black and one white.


01:15:57.554 --> 01:15:58.998
So distracting.


01:15:59.255 --> 01:16:01.757
Was it just a gimmick? A trick?


01:16:01.758 --> 01:16:03.931
Cass, I... I don't know what
you're talking about, okay?


01:16:04.260 --> 01:16:06.706
A trick you don't need sounds so funny.


01:16:06.996 --> 01:16:09.533
Yes, gimmick's a better word.


01:16:09.732 --> 01:16:11.200
Irrelevant.


01:16:11.201 --> 01:16:13.647
We were so good we didn't need gimmicks.


01:16:14.304 --> 01:16:16.215
A promise was made.


01:16:16.973 --> 01:16:19.043
Was that promise kept?


01:16:23.580 --> 01:16:26.060
They arranged this so
that I would be happy.


01:16:26.549 --> 01:16:29.051
They'll do anything to keep me happy.


01:16:29.219 --> 01:16:32.598
Anything. I'm so precious to them.


01:16:34.390 --> 01:16:36.028
I have to go.


01:16:36.626 --> 01:16:38.160
I... I have to go.


01:16:38.161 --> 01:16:39.435
What? No.


01:16:39.729 --> 01:16:41.096
- You can't do it. Please, Dad,
- No!


01:16:41.097 --> 01:16:42.231
- No! No. I don't...
- you can't tell anybody.


01:16:42.232 --> 01:16:43.599
- No I'm gonna tell...
- Promise me, Daddy.


01:16:43.600 --> 01:16:45.701
- I'm telling the police. You're coming with me.
- You have to pretend it's all a dream.


01:16:45.702 --> 01:16:48.036
- You'll never see me again.
- You're coming to see your mother. I...


01:16:48.037 --> 01:16:49.738
- No! Daddy, no!
- I've got you in my hands.


01:16:49.739 --> 01:16:51.340
...you're not going anywhere.
You understand me?


01:16:51.341 --> 01:16:52.148
No.


01:16:52.475 --> 01:16:53.976
No.


01:16:55.678 --> 01:16:57.112
- No.
- Cass...


01:16:57.113 --> 01:16:58.853
Daddy.


01:16:59.415 --> 01:17:02.088
- Daddy.
- Cass.


01:17:09.192 --> 01:17:11.933
Okay, boys, show's over.


01:17:13.329 --> 01:17:15.001
Go on, now.


01:17:16.633 --> 01:17:19.010
He'll be conscious in ten minutes.


01:17:29.512 --> 01:17:31.616
All right, Cassandra.


01:17:34.450 --> 01:17:37.328
Alright, now.


01:17:38.755 --> 01:17:41.257
It's time to go home. Yeah.


01:17:43.059 --> 01:17:46.096
Cassandra, let's go home.


01:17:47.030 --> 01:17:52.809
All right. All right. All right.


01:17:54.938 --> 01:17:56.781
Come on, sweetie.


01:17:57.507 --> 01:17:58.917
That's it.


01:18:00.009 --> 01:18:01.647
That's it.


01:18:04.480 --> 01:18:09.122
Detective, I really hope you don't
think I was avoiding your phone calls.


01:18:09.419 --> 01:18:13.488
It's just that I have spoken already
to two other colleagues of yours.


01:18:13.489 --> 01:18:15.093
Yeah, I understand that.


01:18:15.258 --> 01:18:16.592
As I told them,


01:18:16.593 --> 01:18:21.166
I have no idea how this woman would
find her way into our charity ball.


01:18:21.397 --> 01:18:24.299
You have to understand that this
is a very well-publicized event.


01:18:24.300 --> 01:18:25.834
Tell me, what was your your contact


01:18:25.835 --> 01:18:27.973
with the woman after
she came to your table?


01:18:28.304 --> 01:18:30.472
I hardly spoke with her.


01:18:30.473 --> 01:18:34.109
There was only one empty
chair in the whole room


01:18:34.110 --> 01:18:36.851
and she took that empty seat.


01:18:36.913 --> 01:18:40.582
You see, Detective Dunlop was
supposed to come with a guest.


01:18:40.583 --> 01:18:41.993
Yeah. We...


01:18:46.656 --> 01:18:49.558
She decided that she...
she wanted to go alone.


01:18:49.559 --> 01:18:51.936
- So you...?
- Yeah.


01:18:54.631 --> 01:19:00.709
Could this mystery woman have somehow
known that you weren't coming?


01:19:03.506 --> 01:19:04.673
I'm sorry, you're the detective.


01:19:04.674 --> 01:19:06.541
Can you tell me anything
more about this woman?


01:19:06.542 --> 01:19:08.612
Any details, anything at all?


01:19:09.679 --> 01:19:11.852
Did you see them leave together?


01:19:11.981 --> 01:19:13.815
I saw the back of them.


01:19:13.816 --> 01:19:17.024
But I was speaking with
someone else at that moment.


01:19:18.454 --> 01:19:21.823
I think I heard the woman
offer Detective Dunlop a ride.


01:19:21.824 --> 01:19:23.962
Didn't that strike you as suspicious?


01:19:24.027 --> 01:19:25.437
Suspicious?


01:19:25.461 --> 01:19:27.863
A stranger offers a
police officer a ride?


01:19:27.864 --> 01:19:29.502
She needed one.


01:19:30.833 --> 01:19:34.007
She was alone, after all.


01:20:08.638 --> 01:20:10.139
Hello?


01:20:11.474 --> 01:20:13.248
Is anyone there?


01:20:14.277 --> 01:20:16.051
Hello?


01:20:23.519 --> 01:20:25.420
Oh, yeah, I know. I know.


01:20:25.421 --> 01:20:27.823
You've been really understanding.
I appreciate that.


01:20:27.824 --> 01:20:29.825
I mean that. Do you have
any idea where she's gone?


01:20:29.826 --> 01:20:31.660
- No.
- Or where she's working now?


01:20:31.661 --> 01:20:34.996
Linda used to make sure that these are
up all the time... it's not up right now.


01:20:35.097 --> 01:20:36.798
- She stopped working here last year.
- I understand that.


01:20:36.899 --> 01:20:39.936
I'm going to put it up
right now, okay? Thank you.


01:21:36.159 --> 01:21:39.594
- What's so funny?
- No, it's not a trick, it's a gimmick.


01:21:39.595 --> 01:21:41.296
A gimmick we don't need.


01:21:41.297 --> 01:21:44.073
That day you lost me.
Was it just a trick?


01:21:44.467 --> 01:21:47.413
Or maybe gimmick's a better word.
One black, one white.


01:21:47.436 --> 01:21:49.905
I made him promise he'll never
skate with anyone else.


01:21:49.906 --> 01:21:53.114
We were so good we didn't need
anything like that to get attention.


01:21:53.376 --> 01:21:55.219
The promise was made.


01:21:55.311 --> 01:21:57.085
Was that promise kept?


01:22:50.633 --> 01:22:55.707
Nicole, just tell me what it was like.


01:22:58.040 --> 01:23:02.249
What was it like to sleep in
an abandoned van on your...


01:23:02.545 --> 01:23:04.991
fourteenth birthday? Yeah?


01:23:06.549 --> 01:23:09.529
Does this remind you
of what it was like?


01:23:10.853 --> 01:23:13.588
Sorry if I got some
of the details wrong.


01:23:13.589 --> 01:23:16.933
But you didn't tell me what
colour the van was so...


01:23:17.293 --> 01:23:20.433
I found the yellow to be quite striking.


01:23:22.198 --> 01:23:32.517
Just tell me, is this anything like
what you experienced, is it?


01:23:35.278 --> 01:23:40.921
Start thinking of the details
or else I might not be back.


01:24:21.090 --> 01:24:23.900
Excuse me, you probably shouldn't...


01:24:28.864 --> 01:24:31.275
What other rooms do you work in?


01:24:31.534 --> 01:24:33.911
Every room on this floor.


01:24:37.940 --> 01:24:39.107
Hey, baby.


01:24:39.108 --> 01:24:41.476
I was wondering if you could
please come to the house?


01:24:41.477 --> 01:24:43.979
- Come home?
- We need to talk.


01:24:44.313 --> 01:24:45.951
Talk about what?


01:24:46.015 --> 01:24:47.391
Just come to the house.


01:24:47.450 --> 01:24:50.658
Okay. It's gonna take me a few hours.
I'm gonna be right there.


01:24:51.020 --> 01:24:53.227
- Three cameras found.
- Can't trace the uplink yet.


01:24:54.256 --> 01:24:56.497
- In all the rooms that Tina works?
- Yeah.


01:24:57.460 --> 01:25:01.464
- Alright, what's going on? Ideas?
- Yeah. Some kind of thrill crime.


01:25:01.864 --> 01:25:03.308
What's the thrill?


01:25:03.466 --> 01:25:05.100
Watching mummy twist.


01:25:05.101 --> 01:25:07.103
It's actually not a bad
idea for a reality show.


01:25:07.303 --> 01:25:09.504
Look it, it's out there, I know,
but listen, you got the kid.


01:25:09.505 --> 01:25:13.808
So why not watch the mother's pain
and confusion? A blank trophy.


01:25:13.809 --> 01:25:17.679
- A teacup. Throw in some baby teeth.
- A hairbrush. A pinwheel.


01:25:17.680 --> 01:25:18.947
Eight years after the abduction?


01:25:18.948 --> 01:25:20.515
Hey, they might have
been watching all along.


01:25:20.516 --> 01:25:23.121
The personality driven to abduct
the child, we're used to.


01:25:25.788 --> 01:25:28.290
Noticing a mother's quiet desperation.


01:25:29.592 --> 01:25:31.127
That's something else.


01:25:31.560 --> 01:25:33.194
What are you saying, Sam?


01:25:33.195 --> 01:25:37.132
There's a kidnapper
and there's a watcher.


01:25:37.133 --> 01:25:38.433
Or watchers.


01:25:38.434 --> 01:25:40.709
Maybe even subscribers.


01:25:40.836 --> 01:25:42.940
A whole new class of freaks.


01:25:43.539 --> 01:25:45.017
Let's go.


01:25:50.713 --> 01:25:52.157
Hi.


01:25:55.217 --> 01:25:57.025
Hello, Matthew.


01:25:57.153 --> 01:25:58.825
What's going on?


01:25:59.255 --> 01:26:01.325
Let's talk for a minute.


01:26:02.625 --> 01:26:06.368
Well, I don't... I don't really
have anything to say.


01:26:09.298 --> 01:26:10.799
Please?


01:26:21.310 --> 01:26:23.756
Nicole thinks that they might be...


01:26:24.880 --> 01:26:26.984
they might be watching me.


01:26:29.051 --> 01:26:30.552
Who's watching you?


01:26:30.553 --> 01:26:33.590
It looks like the abductors
aren't so far out of the picture.


01:26:34.590 --> 01:26:37.434
Nicole found some cameras in
my rooms that were hidden.


01:26:37.693 --> 01:26:38.593
Why?


01:26:38.594 --> 01:26:41.301
We'd love any ideas you have about that.


01:26:41.397 --> 01:26:42.967
Well, I have no idea.


01:26:44.433 --> 01:26:48.938
Did you keep any of Case's teeth,
her baby teeth?


01:26:50.339 --> 01:26:51.773
What?


01:26:51.774 --> 01:26:54.275
Tina's found some baby teeth


01:26:54.276 --> 01:26:57.780
- and some other things in the rooms.
- Other things? What other things?


01:26:58.347 --> 01:27:02.021
A trophy. Like the one she won.


01:27:02.051 --> 01:27:03.928
The teeth?


01:27:04.553 --> 01:27:08.089
- Okay, are they hers?
- Why would you think they were hers?


01:27:08.090 --> 01:27:10.934
If they're not hers, then why the
fuck are we talking about them?


01:27:13.596 --> 01:27:16.303
I'm not saying... I'm not saying
anything else with this...


01:27:16.398 --> 01:27:18.969
Get outta my house. Go.


01:27:35.351 --> 01:27:37.023
What do you want from me?


01:27:38.320 --> 01:27:41.960
The teeth were placed in the rooms,


01:27:42.391 --> 01:27:43.758
under the pillows.


01:27:43.759 --> 01:27:45.426
I found them like they were
left for the Tooth Fairy.


01:27:45.427 --> 01:27:47.497
You know, like we used
to do with Cassie.


01:27:47.930 --> 01:27:49.797
Have you asked the Tooth Fairy?


01:27:49.798 --> 01:27:52.433
- Do you think this is funny?
- Yeah. A little. I do. How...


01:27:52.434 --> 01:27:54.106
how long has this been going on, hon?


01:27:54.503 --> 01:27:56.607
How come no one's told me?


01:27:56.739 --> 01:28:00.844
Tina, why tell me, right?
Why ask for my help.


01:28:00.945 --> 01:28:03.982
You guys are doing great on your own.
It's only been eight years.


01:28:04.079 --> 01:28:07.148
You people can't even do your job.
All you can do is turn my wife against me.


01:28:07.149 --> 01:28:10.118
Tina, do you think that I did this?
Is that what you think? That I went in there,


01:28:10.119 --> 01:28:14.692
I put a bunch of... cameras in there?
And then... and what? And what?


01:28:20.896 --> 01:28:22.670
Tina.


01:28:26.936 --> 01:28:30.506
Mr. Lane, is there something
you're not telling us?


01:28:31.106 --> 01:28:34.052
No! No!


01:28:34.810 --> 01:28:36.411
So now what?


01:28:36.412 --> 01:28:38.892
You gonna arrest me?
Go ahead, please do it.


01:28:39.181 --> 01:28:43.652
Please. If you think that I did this, you...
you come here and you arrest me.


01:29:05.474 --> 01:29:06.975
What's with the shrine here, man?


01:29:25.794 --> 01:29:28.365
It's just there's so
many people from before.


01:29:28.597 --> 01:29:33.068
There's Jill from my soccer team.
My best friend, Karen. Albert.


01:29:34.103 --> 01:29:36.913
And now that I can't see
my mum anymore I need...


01:29:36.972 --> 01:29:40.009
new experiences.
I need to feel inspired.


01:29:42.111 --> 01:29:43.678
Oh, yeah.


01:29:43.679 --> 01:29:47.058
Do you remember that story
I told you about the trophy?


01:29:47.516 --> 01:29:50.656
About the moment I skated over to
my mother and handed it to her?


01:29:51.420 --> 01:29:54.025
Remember how moved you were?


01:29:54.957 --> 01:29:57.027
I want to feel that.


01:29:57.660 --> 01:30:00.663
You told me it was the best
story I ever told you.


01:30:01.897 --> 01:30:03.671
It was.


01:30:04.433 --> 01:30:06.879
So why don't we make it even better?


01:30:09.705 --> 01:30:11.309
How?


01:30:31.260 --> 01:30:34.395
I'm just wondering if you kept
that trophy or if Cass kept it.


01:30:34.396 --> 01:30:36.698
- What's this for?
- It's just for an article I'm writing about


01:30:36.699 --> 01:30:40.068
children who disappear and the impact
that it has years later on the...


01:30:40.069 --> 01:30:41.969
This article sounds
like fucking bullshit.


01:30:41.970 --> 01:30:44.339
- No, it's not. It's very serious...
- What, you come here eight years later


01:30:44.340 --> 01:30:45.573
and then bring up Cass?


01:30:45.574 --> 01:30:48.676
I'm just wondering about the impact that
it had on your life. I'm wondering...


01:30:48.677 --> 01:30:50.912
Yeah, it impacted my life.
What do you want to know?


01:30:50.913 --> 01:30:52.480
I want to know about this
trophy that you won.


01:30:52.481 --> 01:30:54.517
- I wondered if you kept it.
- No. No.


01:30:55.217 --> 01:30:56.951
I'm done. No, this is fucking bullshit.


01:30:56.952 --> 01:30:59.432
- Did you keep the trophy?
- Yeah, I kept the fucking trophy.


01:31:00.022 --> 01:31:01.456
Okay. I can...
I can see that you're upset.


01:31:01.457 --> 01:31:02.990
- I won't ask you any more questions.
- Great. Are we done?


01:31:02.991 --> 01:31:05.835
- Yeah. Thank you very much for your time.
- Awesome. Thank you so much.


01:31:24.580 --> 01:31:25.888
Albert?


01:31:26.915 --> 01:31:28.120
Who's that?


01:31:28.450 --> 01:31:31.021
Some creepy bitch asking about Cass.


01:33:30.439 --> 01:33:32.273
- Yeah?
- I don't know who's in charge here anymore.


01:33:32.274 --> 01:33:35.343
I used to deal with Nicole Dunlop.
'kay... This is urgent.


01:33:35.344 --> 01:33:37.778
- Who is this?
- Matthew Lane.


01:33:37.779 --> 01:33:39.013
Matthew Lane.


01:33:39.014 --> 01:33:42.383
- Case's father. Cass Lane.
- Yeah, I know who you are, Matthew.


01:33:42.384 --> 01:33:45.119
I've found them. Those people who
took my daughter, I found them.


01:33:45.120 --> 01:33:46.928
They're at a diner on Route 15.


01:33:46.955 --> 01:33:49.264
You been watching a lot
of movies, lately, Matthew?


01:33:49.791 --> 01:33:53.966
Listen to me.
These people have my daughter.


01:33:54.062 --> 01:33:57.338
I've seen her. I've been...
I've been with her.


01:33:58.700 --> 01:34:00.508
She's alive.


01:34:01.737 --> 01:34:04.505
Hey. I need you to listen
to me very carefully.


01:34:04.506 --> 01:34:07.808
I have a phone and the phone has GPS.
I'm gonna plant it on their car.


01:34:07.809 --> 01:34:08.876
I'll give you the number.


01:34:08.877 --> 01:34:11.379
I'm gonna plant it on their car
and then you can track it.


01:34:11.380 --> 01:34:15.925
And then you can find them in case
something happens to me, okay?


01:34:49.351 --> 01:34:52.627
Do you mind if I...
if I ask you a few questions?


01:34:52.921 --> 01:34:55.332
- About what?
- About Cass Lane.


01:34:55.991 --> 01:34:59.360
- Okay.
- Yeah, I... I'm writing an article about...


01:34:59.361 --> 01:35:02.697
children who disappear and the effect
that it has on the people in their lives.


01:35:02.698 --> 01:35:04.370
Yeah.


01:35:05.901 --> 01:35:09.439
- Just got a call from Matthew Lane.
- Yeah, I overheard you.


01:35:10.038 --> 01:35:12.040
What is it with you and that guy?


01:35:15.477 --> 01:35:17.854
Says he met this guy at a diner.


01:35:18.113 --> 01:35:20.781
Thinks he's the one that
stole his daughter.


01:35:20.782 --> 01:35:23.262
So he tossed his cell
phone in the guy's car.


01:35:24.553 --> 01:35:26.054
Want me to check it out?


01:35:27.489 --> 01:35:28.899
Yeah.


01:35:38.600 --> 01:35:40.602
Hey! Put that back!


01:35:40.736 --> 01:35:44.115
- It's my daughter.
- I don't care who it is, I said put it back!


01:35:46.675 --> 01:35:48.576
Do you want me to call the cops?


01:35:48.577 --> 01:35:50.556
Yeah, I want you to call the cops.


01:35:50.912 --> 01:35:53.221
Do it. Do it.


01:36:16.338 --> 01:36:18.044
Have you seen this girl?


01:36:19.508 --> 01:36:23.455
I lost her a few miles from here,
at a diner just like this one.


01:36:24.413 --> 01:36:26.221
That's awful.


01:36:27.949 --> 01:36:30.019
Yeah, it's awful.


01:36:31.420 --> 01:36:34.730
I went in to get a and I
